<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  macOS hardened-runtime entitlements for the lets-chat desktop bundle.

  Tauri enables the hardened runtime by default (bundle.macOS.hardenedRuntime).
  Under the hardened runtime a signed app cannot reach device capture APIs
  unless it also carries the matching entitlements, even when the Info.plist
  usage strings are present. These entitlements are inert until the codesign
  step runs, which only happens on the macOS build path owned by LC-126
  (currently parked for lack of macOS hardware + Apple credentials). On
  Linux / Windows builds this file is ignored.

  LC-137: getDisplayMedia (screen share). WKWebView gained getDisplayMedia in
  macOS 13. The WebKit-layer consent is auto-granted by wry's
  WryWebViewUIDelegate (the same delegate that auto-grants getUserMedia), so
  there is no Rust-side permission hook to install in src/main.rs. What the
  hardened runtime requires is the screen-capture entitlement below; the
  OS-level Screen Recording (TCC) prompt is then raised automatically by
  macOS the first time a call requests display capture and remembered across
  launches (no Info.plist usage string controls the Screen Recording prompt).

  LC-134 (getUserMedia, camera + microphone) adds the
  com.apple.security.device.camera and com.apple.security.device.audio-input
  entitlements to this same file. If both land independently, union the keys:
  this file should carry camera, audio-input, AND screen-capture.

  LC-126 may extend this file with the remaining signing entitlements WebKit
  needs under the hardened runtime (e.g. com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.device.screen-capture</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
